- `moon_pdk_api` v2.0.4 — core request/response structs (`RegisterExtensionInput/Output`, `ExecuteExtensionInput`, `MoonContext`, etc.)
- `moon_pdk` v2.0.4 — depends on `moon_pdk_api`, `moon_common`, `moon_project`, `moon_task`, `extism-pdk`, and `warpgate_pdk`. Provides `load_project`, `load_task`, `load_extension_config` helpers via `#[host_fn] extern "ExtismHost" { fn load_project_by_id... }` in `crates/pdk/src/funcs.rs`.

The `exec_command!` macro/host-fn plugins actually need for shelling out to `git` etc. lives one layer down, in **`warpgate_pdk`** (moonrepo/proto repo, `crates/warpgate-pdk`, current version 0.16.5, moon v2.4.6 pins `warpgate_pdk = "0.16.4"` per moon's root `Cargo.toml`). Declaration (`crates/warpgate-pdk/src/funcs.rs`):
```rust
#[host_fn]
extern "ExtismHost" {
    fn exec_command(input: Json<ExecCommandInput>) -> Json<ExecCommandOutput>;
}
```
Call site pattern (`crates/warpgate-pdk/src/macros.rs`, `funcs.rs`):
```rust
pub fn exec_captured<C: AsRef<str>, I: IntoIterator<Item=A>, A: AsRef<str>>(command: C, args: I) -> AnyResult<ExecCommandOutput> {
    exec(ExecCommandInput::pipe(command, args))
}
// internally: unsafe { exec_command(Json(input))?.0 }
```
So a plugin never calls `std::process::Command` directly (WASM has no process spawn) — it must call `warpgate_pdk::exec_captured("git", ["status", ...])` which round-trips through the host via Extism's `#[host_fn]` FFI. `callisto-moon`'s `runner.rs` uses `std::process::Command::new(program).output()` directly (`crates/callisto-moon/src/runner.rs:9-13`), which will not compile/run correctly for `wasm32-unknown-unknown`/`wasip1` under Extism — this is the real, deeper mismatch beyond just struct shapes.

